0result.sql is the correct choice.  
• It explicitly distinguishes “helmet used” from “helmet not used”, matching the task’s two required groups.  
• It filters out records where helmet status is unknown, preventing them from skewing the “no‑helmet” denominator (problem seen in 1result.sql).  
• It counts fatalities with party_number_killed (motorcyclist‑specific) and divides by the number of DISTINCT collisions for each group, exactly what the task asks.  
• 2result.sql mis‑classifies many collisions (very small denominator / 0 fatalities for no‑helmet) because it relies on collisions.motorcyclist_killed_count after creating overlapping case sets, giving implausible rates.  

